Awami Nastaliq is a Nastaliq-style Arabic script font supporting a wide
variety of languages of South Asia, including but not limited to Urdu. This
font is aimed at minority language support.

Lesser-known languages often require more vowel diacritics than Urdu. They
may use a different set of base characters and diacritics, and the base
characters often include more nuqtas to represent sounds that are not
present in Urdu or standard Arabic. Awami Nastaliq includes all the vowel
diacritics and base characters required for languages using the Nastaliq
style of Arabic script. This makes it unique among Nastaliq fonts.
